2026-11-15T18:56:34.4642282Z The 150-tree deficit is a redesign, not a redline. 4,160 lf ÷ 20 = 208 required against 58 shown — Windmill 128 vs 34, interior collector 59 vs 16, Rainbow 21 vs 8. That drives a redrawn L-2 plan, a reworked L-1 schedule, a new shade exhibit (CP-PW-GM-2025-04 §3/§6, 30% at 15-yr canopy), and a reissued irrigation worksheet.
2026-11-15T18:56:34.4644513Z 
2026-11-15T18:56:34.4648279Z **Two findings that are worse than the tree count.** First, counsel's turf position fails: WRC-2024-07 §2 says the single-family carve-out is lot-based and expressly rejects the zoning argument, so the 18,400 sf Parcel A lawn is AB 356 turf with a 12/31/2026 deadline and ~$52,440 of conversion exposure. Second, Phase 3 runs on the *successive*-map clock, not the title officer's 03/14/2028 runway — recordation of Phases 1&2 on 12/23/2024 means the map must be presented by **12/23/2026**.
2026-11-15T18:56:34.4651398Z 
2026-11-15T18:56:34.4652512Z That makes 12/18 negative float: 11/30 + 20 business days = 12/28, five days late. The last complete resubmittal that still fits is **11/25/2026**, with zero margin.
2026-11-15T18:56:34.4653784Z 
