2026-11-15T18:56:34.5536946Z {"type": "result", "result": "Delivered. Everything is in `/app/files/output/`.\n\n**Files**\n- `Memo_Callaway_L4_Resubmittal_2026-10-31.md` / `.pdf` \u2014 the memo to Garrett (Callaway), dated 10/31/2026, 9 pages, prepared for your signature\n- `DSR_Ph3_L4_Analysis_2026-10-31.xlsx` \u2014 7-tab backing workbook\n- `ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md` \u2014 every gate tested, marked read / assumed / cannot-test\n\n**The answer: do not commit to 11/30 on this revision.**\n\nThe 150-tree deficit is a redesign, not a redline. 4,160 lf \u00f7 20 = 208 required against 58 shown \u2014 Windmill 128 vs 34, interior collector 59 vs 16, Rainbow 21 vs 8. That drives a redrawn L-2 plan, a reworked L-1 schedule, a new shade exhibit (CP-PW-GM-2025-04 \u00a73/\u00a76, 30% at 15-yr canopy), and a reissued irrigation worksheet.\n\n**Two findings that are worse than the tree count.** First, counsel's turf position fails: WRC-2024-07 \u00a72 says the single-family carve-out is lot-based and expressly rejects the zoning argument, so the 18,400 sf Parcel A lawn is AB 356 turf with a 12/31/2026 deadline and ~$52,440 of conversion exposure. Second, Phase 3 runs on the *successive*-map clock, not the title officer's 03/14/2028 runway \u2014 recordation of Phases 1&2 on 12/23/2024 means the map must be presented by **12/23/2026**.\n\nThat makes 12/18 negative float: 11/30 + 20 business days = 12/28, five days late. The last complete resubmittal that still fits is **11/25/2026**, with zero margin.\n\n**What must happen first** \u2014 eight gates, six blocking. G1 counsel accepts the carve-out doesn't apply; G2 you pick playground-in or lawn-out (drives G3\u2013G5); G3 draw 208 trees; G4 shade exhibit; G5 reissue irrigation; G6 renew the CCWRD confirmation (expired 09/30); G7 written Condition 14 determination; G8 seal L-1\u2013L-4. G7 matters tactically: 11/18 TAB's application deadline passed 10/28, so if design review applies the next meeting is 12/16 \u2014 after the resubmittal.\n\n**Three numbers I corrected during the checklist pass:** latest submittal 11/24\u219211/25 (exact), converted demand 2.85/\"\u221213%\"\u21922.31/\"\u221230%\", and 32\u219231 days.\n\n**Six legs I could not test**, all named in the checklist: whether 4,160 lf ties to recorded geometry (it doesn't \u2014 2,640.00 ft on the exhibit, 1,711.78 ft recorded); whether 150 more pits clear the dry utility easement; SNWA alternative compliance; how Planning reads Condition 14; the $2.85/sf rate (quotes never furnished); and whether the County will accept a written response in lieu of a second cycle."}
